  "body": "Background batch gate on main at 9bc121f is red, and still red at 8b3163d: `lathe_field_sim::profile_rough_and_finish_simulate_with_meridian_parity` panics at lathe_field_sim.rs:147 with `the field eye cuts the lathe program: \"PR1: inputs moved since generation - regenerate before posting\"`.\n\nLikely cause (not bisected): an interaction between PR #165 (#156: the stock term in every part- or selection-sourced op's stamp) and PR #135 (#103: the turning laws and the prior collected for turning ops), or PR #153 (#109: the ahead-ops digest). Either the fixture sets or changes the stock after generating, which now stales PR1, or an op's stamp digests something that generation itself changes. #135's last merge of main was tested on a suite list that did not include lathe_field_sim.\n\nDone means: find which input moved. If it's the fixture's order (stock set after generate), fix the fixture. If generation changes an input its own stamp reads, so the op is Stale right after generating, fix that: it's a real bug that would hit users. Pin with the test green and, in the second case, a direct test that a freshly generated lathe op reads Ok.\n\nLogs: gate-logs/batch-20261107-234911 in the main checkout.",
